    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_dc18a5170602b7b50aec05f8e670303ee675646dbf36984a0dc5280c3f95819b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source exposes a model-identification gap between bulk and tails. Conditioning Gram-block types on block length reveals drifting, approximately paired or convex-looking frequency shapes and inadequate samples for longer blocks, whereas rare configurations are recorded through different local observables: exception type, S extrema, normalized zero gaps, and Z amplitude. The requested probabilistic model directly targets the type distributions; connecting that model to the separate tail observables remains an additional bridge the source does not make.",
