    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f08f6f8ec71bcaf90801bc996ad5e7c72d5d218c8193418c9b25e0ad48e90cf0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source separates a proof-facing dependency from an audit layer: method-specific error envelopes turn computed Z values into certified signs; those signs support zero separation and, with the cited endpoint/counting theorem, the finite-height conclusion. Exact reruns, overlapping comparisons, and the Gram-interval count identity then audit bookkeeping and exception handling, so these checks strengthen the computation without all being stated as logical premises of the theorem.",
